.TH geectl-build-check-constraints 1  "geectl-build-check-constraints 0.2.2" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-build\-check\-constraints \- List the worker ids satisfying a `_constraints` document
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl build check\-constraints\fR [\fB\-\-constraints\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> <\fIPACKAGE\fR> <\fIREPOSITORY\fR> <\fIARCH\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
List the worker ids satisfying a `_constraints` document
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-constraints\fR \fI<CONSTRAINTS>\fR
The constraints document, as authored. Without it, an empty body is posted, which the server accepts
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project the package is in
.TP
<\fIPACKAGE\fR>
The package to check the constraints for
.TP
<\fIREPOSITORY\fR>
The repository the package builds in
.TP
<\fIARCH\fR>
The architecture the package builds for
.SH VERSION
v0.2.2
